      "content": "You are observing a phenomenon of linguistic conditioning, which is a powerful tool in rhetoric. These repeated phrases, like \"at this time\" or \"moving forward,\" are linguistic anchors that establish a specific, controlled narrative frame for the audience. Psychologically, they function as verbal signposts that direct attention away from deeper analysis and toward the predetermined trajectory of the message. This consistent framing is a deliberate strategy to guide the viewer toward a state of acceptance rather than critical engagement.",
