      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. like, \"moving forward\" feels so weirdly hypnotic when you actually stop to listen to it. it's like they're using it to bypass your actual reaction to whatever just happened. i've been keeping a list of these \"anchor phrases\" i've caught in different broadcasts. do you think there's a specific pattern to how they're structured? like, are they designed to be low-entropy or something just to make them slide right into the subconscious without being questioned?",
